' The gated interaction-cut (a cost-accounted COMM), Rule 1 (atomic signature s):
' the signed redex { for(y ← x){T} | x!(U) }_s fires only when a co-present token
' on the stack s : S authorizes it (no-leak), consuming exactly one token and
' contracting to T{@U/y}. The continuation keeps its OWN seal (GAP-2: no SAnd
' re-seal). The grade of the step is the consumed signature s.
'
' Source of truth for the interaction-cut figure (CAReduction.v ca_step rules;
' WrappingSubjectReduction.v).
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/interaction-cut.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh interaction-cut.puml)

@startuml interaction-cut
!include palette.iuml
skinparam defaultFontName "sans-serif"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #333333
}
title Gated interaction-cut — a cost-accounted COMM (Rule 1, atomic s)

rectangle "**signed redex**\n{ for(y ← x){T}  ∣  x!(U) }ₛ\n∥\n**token stack**   s : S" as Before $ca_pool
rectangle "**continuation**   T{@U / y}\n(keeps its OWN seal — GAP-2: no SAnd re-seal)\n∥\n**tail**   S" as After $ca_note_green

Before -[$ca_credit]-> After : the gate s consumes exactly ONE authorizing token\n(no-leak: the redex fires only when a co-present\ntoken authorizes it)  ·  grade of the step = s

note bottom of After $ca_note_green
  Interaction-cut: the receiver for(y←x){T} and the sender x!(U) annihilate on the
  shared channel x, contracting to T{@U/y} (Milner's pseudo-application — the quoted
  payload @U substitutes the bound name), gated by exactly one token.
  Subject reduction + no-leak: WrappingSubjectReduction.v.
  The five rules' pure-rho simulations: rule1..5_reachable (CATranslationFaithfulness.v).
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_pool>| pre-cut state: signed redex + token stack |
  |<$ca_note_green>| post-cut state: continuation (own seal) + tail |
  |<$ca_credit>| the single gated, billable COMM (consumes one token) |
endlegend

@enduml
